    {
      "term": "Shine Usu",
      "matchText": "Shine Usu",
      "type": "concept",
      "definition": "One of two great inscribed stelae left by the Uyghur qaghan Bayanchur (the other is the Tariat inscription), found at Shine Usu in Mongolia and cut in runiform Old Turkic. It narrates his campaigns and the founding of the khaganate in the Uyghurs' own voice — a rare inside source for a people otherwise seen through their enemies' records."
    },
    {
      "term": "Tariat",
      "matchText": "Tariat",
      "type": "concept",
      "definition": "A monumental Old Turkic inscription raised by the Uyghur qaghan Bayanchur (also called the Terkhin inscription), companion to the Shine Usu stele. Together they are the Uyghur Khaganate's own runiform account of its founding and wars — the thin counter-voice to the Chinese histories that otherwise narrate the steppe."
    },
