      "term": "Sogdian",
      "matchText": "Sogdian",
      "type": "people",
      "definition": "An Iranian-speaking people of the oasis cities of Samarkand and Bukhara (in modern Uzbekistan) whose caravan networks were the commercial nervous system of Inner Asia. Sogdians served as merchants, scribes, financiers, and diplomats across the steppe world for centuries."
