    {
      "term": "jut",
      "matchText": "the steppe's specific terror",
      "type": "concept",
      "definition": "A catastrophic winter event on the Eurasian steppe, when ice crusts seal the grass beneath and livestock cannot graze, causing mass die-offs within days. A single severe jut could wipe out the herds that were a nomad army's horses, food supply, and currency all at once — the specific vulnerability a fixed-capital empire could not survive the way a dispersed nomadic one might."
    },
