      "term": "Wang Yande",
      "matchText": "Wang Yande",
      "type": "person",
      "definition": "A Song Chinese diplomat who visited the Uyghur Kingdom of Qocho in 981–984 and left a detailed written account of what he saw: irrigated fields, Buddhist monasteries, libraries, and a literate court. His report is one of the clearest eyewitness portraits of a nomad people who had, within two or three generations, become a settled agrarian civilization."
