    {
      "term": "ortoq",
      "matchText": "ortoq",
      "type": "concept",
      "definition": "A Central Asian capital-pooling trade partnership in which investors — merchants, nobles, even rulers — entrusted silver or silk to a traveling merchant and shared the profits on the caravan's return. The Uyghurs of Qocho ran ortoq networks across the Silk Road; when the Mongol Empire emerged it adopted the institution empire-wide as the *ortogh*, the commercial system that tied the Mongols' vast territories into a single trade network."
    },
